`tally` writes memory its caller can see at tests/wordings/nl2345_par_shared_write_map_into.ts:10:3, and `parallelMapInto` runs it on several threads at once: a parallel body may read what its caller owns and write nothing but its result; make it answer what it computes and do the write after the call, or run it on the thread that called it, `for (let i = 0; i < src.length; i++) { dst[i] = tally(src[i]) }`
